      ro: "",
      en: "The Gettysburg Battlefield in Pennsylvania marks the site of the bloodiest and most consequential engagement of the American Civil War. Fought over three sweltering days from July 1 to 3, 1863, Union Major General George Meade's Army of the Potomac successfully halted the second and final Northern invasion by Confederate General Robert E. Lee's Army of Northern Virginia. The battle culminated on the third day with the disastrous Confederate infantry assault famously known as Pickett's Charge, which was decisively repulsed by the Union center. The staggering combined total of roughly 50,000 casualties devastated both armies. Later that year, President Abraham Lincoln delivered his immortal Gettysburg Address here, dedicating the site's national cemetery. History K8 â€” the turning point of the Civil War."
