      ro: "",
      en: "Madison Square Garden, commonly abbreviated as MSG, is a massive multi-purpose indoor arena located in Midtown Manhattan, New York City, situated directly atop Pennsylvania Station. The current structure, which opened in 1968, is actually the fourth venue to bear the famous name. Self-proclaimed as 'The World's Most Famous Arena', it is the prestigious home court for both the New York Knicks (NBA) and the New York Rangers (NHL). Beyond professional sports, the 20,000-seat venue has hosted a legendary array of historic events, including monumental boxing matches like the first Ali-Frazier fight, massive political conventions, and spectacular concerts by the biggest names in the global music industry. Cultural Studies K7 â€” urban entertainment complexes."
